---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/url';
import { breadcrumbJsonLd } from '../../lib/seo';
import bubbleBoardImage from '../../assets/projects/bubble-board/bubble-board.png';
const title = 'Bubble board';
const description = 'Interactive touch-table software designed to support collaborative group activities';
const jsonLd = [breadcrumbJsonLd([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Projects', path: '/projects/' }, { name: title, path: '/projects/bubble-board/' }], Astro.site)];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <PageHeader title={title} />
  <article class="container bubble-board">
    <a class="back-link" href={href('/projects/')}>← Projects</a>
    <figure>
      <Image src={bubbleBoardImage} widths={[720, 1200, 1800]} sizes="(min-width: 60em) 56rem, 92vw" alt="Bubble Board illustration showing people collaborating around a shared touch-table" loading="eager" />
    </figure>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>The Bubble Board is envisioned as a modular platform for dialogue-based Hybrid Intelligence. It is an interactive touch-table designed to support collaborative group activities, such as brainstorming, reflection, and group decision-making through dialogue. The current system captures spoken discussion, extracts ideas, and displays them as editable bubbles on a shared interface. Crucially, the Bubble Board is not intended as a stand-alone application, but as a platform to which further modules can be added, such as knowledge-graph reasoning, value annotation, reinforcement-learning-based idea structuring, or links to VR and other interaction environments</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .bubble-board { display: grid; gap: var(--space-l); padding-bottom: var(--space-xl); }
  .back-link { justify-self: start; }
  figure { margin: 0; max-width: 56rem; }
  figure img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); }
</style>
